{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015MVdCfhSsWu6uTzrKowkCv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL 2026 and reviewing processes, though the specific detailed reviewer guidelines document for CoRL 2026 doesn't appear to be fully available yet. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Overview\n\nCoRL 2026 will be held in Austin, Texas, US. The conference aims to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer. They are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ ICRA/ IROS/ RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/ NeurIPS/ ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\n## Review Process Insights\n\nWhile I didn't find the specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines document, I found reference to CoRL 2024 reviewer instructions which indicate that submissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nFor more detailed and current reviewer guidelines and the official review form for CoRL 2026, you may want to check the OpenReview portal directly at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference or visit the main CoRL 2026 website at https://www.corl.org/\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e6dd661-5539-4780-b46e-9be6f0e5cc6e","uuid":"6ffab08f-059a-4536-83a3-8f0469ef4604","timestamp":"2026-05-26T03:25:41.101Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Y93rtxEvo5AZaz5yWLDVEp","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL 2026 and reviewing processes, though the specific detailed reviewer guidelines document for CoRL 2026 doesn't appear to be fully available yet. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Overview\n\nCoRL 2026 will be held in Austin, Texas, US. The conference aims to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer. They are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ ICRA/ IROS/ RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/ NeurIPS/ ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\n## Review Process Insights\n\nWhile I didn't find the specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines document, I found reference to CoRL 2024 reviewer instructions which indicate that submissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nFor more detailed and current reviewer guidelines and the official review form for CoRL 2026, you may want to check the OpenReview portal directly at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference or visit the main CoRL 2026 website at https://www.corl.org/"],"durationSeconds":5.356694079}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PayfSL32CfRisfc46eDNHg","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 review form scoring rubric acceptance rate\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Survey - Speaker Deck\",\"url\":\"https://speakerdeck.com/harukiabe/corl-2025-survey\"},{\"title\":\"The AI Review Lottery: Widespread AI-Assisted Peer Reviews Boost Paper   Scores and Acceptance Rates\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2405.02150\"},{\"title\":\"What Drives Paper Acceptance? A Process-Centric Analysis of Modern Peer Review\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.25701\"},{\"title\":\"Development and Validation of a Scoring Rubric for Editorial Evaluation of Peer-review Quality: A Pilot Study\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11000557/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Can LLM feedback enhance review quality? A randomized study of 20K   reviews at ICLR 2025\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.09737\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found limited specific information about CoRL 2025's review form scoring rubric and acceptance rate. Here's what I found:\n\nThe search results show that CoRL 2025 was held in Seoul, Korea on September 27-30, 2025, and the conference has already concluded.\n\nHowever, the search results do not contain specific details about:\n- The review form scoring rubric used for CoRL 2025\n- The acceptance rate for CoRL 2025\n\nThe search results mostly returned information about other conferences (like ICLR 2025) and general peer review research, but not the specific details about CoRL 2025's review process and acceptance metrics. To find this information, you may want to check:\n1. The official CoRL 2025 website or their call for papers archive\n2. OpenReview (if CoRL uses this platform)\n3. The conference organizers' official announcements or guidelines\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your res