{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BEy9kdrhKj8uvemiH6Mkft","type":"tool_result","content":"# CoRL 2023 Reviewer Scoring Information\n\nBased on the provided webpage content, **the specific numerical scoring scale, rating dimensions, and confidence levels are not detailed in this document.**\n\nThe guidelines specify evaluation criteria but do not include the actual scoring scale. The review form requests assessments across these dimensions:\n\n- **Originality**: \"Are the problems or methods new?\"\n- **Quality**: \"Is the submission technically sound?\"\n- **Clarity**: \"Is the submission clearly written?\"\n- **Significance**: \"Are the results important?\"\n- **Relevance**: \"Does the paper address a problem in robot learning?\"\n- **Limitations**: Acknowledgment of honestly reported limitations\n\nThe document emphasizes that reviewers should provide \"constructive and concrete\" feedback rather than specifying how to numerically score papers on an overall recommendation scale or confidence scale.\n\nTo obtain the complete scoring rubric with specific numerical values and confidence scales, you would need to access the actual OpenReview review form used during CoRL 2023, which is not included in this guidelines document."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e6dd661-5539-4780-b46e-9be6f0e5cc6e","uuid":"1a23c1a9-ea8b-44b5-b074-63ab7b265834","timestamp":"2026-05-26T03:26:32.499Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":105095,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CoRL 2023 Reviewer Scoring Information\n\nBased on the provided webpage content, **the specific numerical scoring scale, rating dimensions, and confidence levels are not detailed in this document.**\n\nThe guidelines specify evaluation criteria but do not include the actual scoring scale. The review form requests assessments across these dimensions:\n\n- **Originality**: \"Are the problems or methods new?\"\n- **Quality**: \"Is the submission technically sound?\"\n- **Clarity**: \"Is the submission clearly written?\"\n- **Significance**: \"Are the results important?\"\n- **Relevance**: \"Does the paper address a problem in robot learning?\"\n- **Limitations**: Acknowledgment of honestly reported limitations\n\nThe document emphasizes that reviewers should provide \"constructive and concrete\" feedback rather than specifying how to numerically score papers on an overall recommendation scale or confidence scale.\n\nTo obtain the complete scoring rubric with specific numerical values and confidence scales, you would need to access the actual OpenReview review form used during CoRL 2023, which is not included in this guidelines document.","durationMs":6635,"url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"}}
