{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X8jXq2oYyBsVyLr7EXDQ63","type":"tool_result","content":"# CoRL Acceptance Rates and Scoring Scales\n\nBased on the available data:\n\n**CORL 2025** (Seoul, Korea)\n- Acceptance rate: 84.03% (221 accepted out of 263 total)\n- Scoring scale: Not provided\n\n**CORL 2024** (Munich, Germany)\n- Acceptance rate: 39.34% (264 accepted out of 671 total)\n- Scoring scale: 1.70–4.00 (avg: 3.01)\n\n**CORL 2023** (Atlanta, USA)\n- Acceptance rate: 39.96% (199 accepted out of 498 total)\n- Scoring scale: 4.70–10.00 (avg: 6.52)\n\n**CORL 2022**\n- Acceptance rate: 39.09% (197 accepted out of 504 total)\n- Scoring scale: 4.20–10.00 (avg: 6.30)\n\n**CORL 2021**\n- Acceptance rate: 37.50% (153 accepted out of 408 total)\n- Scoring scale: 4.30–10.00 (avg: 6.83)\n\nNotable observation: CORL switched from a 1–10 scoring scale (2021–2023) to a 1–4 scale in 2024. The 2025 acceptance rate appears unusually high at 84%, possibly because those records are still being processed."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e6dd661-5539-4780-b46e-9be6f0e5cc6e","uuid":"13022280-cc80-4880-b6dd-53c3e7b4ae81","timestamp":"2026-05-26T03:27:12.919Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":143480,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CoRL Acceptance Rates and Scoring Scales\n\nBased on the available data:\n\n**CORL 2025** (Seoul, Korea)\n- Acceptance rate: 84.03% (221 accepted out of 263 total)\n- Scoring scale: Not provided\n\n**CORL 2024** (Munich, Germany)\n- Acceptance rate: 39.34% (264 accepted out of 671 total)\n- Scoring scale: 1.70–4.00 (avg: 3.01)\n\n**CORL 2023** (Atlanta, USA)\n- Acceptance rate: 39.96% (199 accepted out of 498 total)\n- Scoring scale: 4.70–10.00 (avg: 6.52)\n\n**CORL 2022**\n- Acceptance rate: 39.09% (197 accepted out of 504 total)\n- Scoring scale: 4.20–10.00 (avg: 6.30)\n\n**CORL 2021**\n- Acceptance rate: 37.50% (153 accepted out of 408 total)\n- Scoring scale: 4.30–10.00 (avg: 6.83)\n\nNotable observation: CORL switched from a 1–10 scoring scale (2021–2023) to a 1–4 scale in 2024. The 2025 acceptance rate appears unusually high at 84%, possibly because those records are still being processed.","durationMs":3913,"url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/"}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TNGpSNZYiA9p5qSBcjieBS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the CoRL scoring information:\n- CoRL 2022-2023: 1-10 scale, ~39-40% acceptance rate\n- CoRL 2024: 1-4 scale (probably: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Accept, 4=Strong Accept or similar), ~39% acceptance rate\n\nSince CoRL 2026 hasn't published its reviewer guidelines yet, I'll use the most recent available — CoRL 2024's scale appears to be 1-4. But the paper also needs context from CoRL 2023 which used 1-10.\n\n\nI'll assume CoRL 2024 uses a 1-4 scale with Strong Accept at 4 down to Strong Reject at 1, maintaining roughly a 39% acceptance rate. The review dimensions typically cover originality, quality, clarity, significance, and relevance to robot learning.\n\nNow I'm ready to dispatch both reviewers in parallel—R1 will focus on methods and experiments while R2 tackles novelty and related work. After they complete their independent assessments, I'll run through the roundtable process: they'll share their initial scores, cross-examine each other's reasoning, converge on key disagreements, and synthesize a final recommendation. I have everything I need to launch both agents.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":708,"cache_read_input_tokens":71342,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":708},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e6dd661-5539-4780-b46e-9be6f0e5cc6e","uuid":"05edce98-473b-4815-8cd9-78da7cdf4bd7"}
