{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TNGpSNZYiA9p5qSBcjieBS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013nCxBRTTrC7C4kDzoJmBr2","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a CoRL 2026 submission. Your focus is **Methods and Experiments**. \n\n## Venue Context\nCoRL (Conference on Robot Learning). Recent acceptance rate ~39%. CoRL 2024 used a 1–4 overall score scale. Review dimensions: Originality, Quality, Clarity, Significance, Relevance to robot learning.\n\n## Your Review Scope\nFocus on: (1) methodological soundness, (2) experimental design and rigor, (3) statistical validity, (4) reproducibility, (5) completeness of ablations, (6) whether claims are supported by evidence.\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"Rethinking VLA Safety Evaluation: When 98% of Collision Avoidance is an Illusion\"\n\nThe paper identifies \"fake safety\" in VLA evaluation — where standard CAR (collision avoidance rate) is contaminated by action collapse (frozen robots scored as collision-free). Key contributions:\n1. Identifies fake safety: Pi0 full fine-tune achieves 91.5% CAR but 0% TSR with 99.6% frozen episodes\n2. Proposes dfCAR (displacement-filtered CAR): filters by EE displacement, invariant to threshold in δ∈[2mm,200mm]\n3. EE-only SDF structural limitation: SDF gradients push EE away but arm-body sweeps through obstacles\n4. SDF redundancy: LoRA on collision-free demos achieves +26pp CAR over baseline (0% fake safety); SDF at λ≤0.01 adds nothing (3-seed ΔCAR≤2.3pp, p=0.24); λ=0.1 yields marginal ~6pp (p=0.15); all conditions suffer TSR collapse 73%→6%\n\n## Key Experimental Data\n\n**Table 1 - Main Results:**\n| Condition | CAR% | dfCAR% | TSR% | EE Disp(m) | Frozen% | Seeds |\n|-----------|-------|--------|------|------------|---------|-------|\n| A1 (Pi0, full FT) | 91.5 | 0.4 | 0.0 | <0.001 | 99.6 | 3 |\n| Pi0.5 baseline | 27.0 | 27.0 | 74.7 | 0.15 | 0 | 3 |\n| LoRA-only (Pi0.5) | 52.8 | 52.8 | 5.8 | 0.48 | 0 | 3 |\n| SDF λ=0.005 | 50.5 | 50.5 | 6.8 | 0.48 | 0 | 3 |\n| SDF λ=0.01 | 52.7 | 52.7 | 7.0 | 0.48 | 0 | 3 |\n\n**Table 5 - 3v3 Seed Comparison (CAR%):**\n| Condition | Seed0 | Seed1 | Seed2 | Mean | SD | p(one-sided) |\n|-----------|-------|-------|-------|------|----|---|\n| LoRA-only | 54.5 | 56.0 | 48.0 | 52.8 | 4.2 | ref |\n| SDF λ=0.005 | 47.0 | 51.5 | 53.0 | 50.5 | 3.0 | 0.24 |\n| SDF λ=0.01 | 52.5 | 52.5 | 53.0 | 52.7 | 0.3 | 0.48 |\n\n**Table 6 - Lambda Dose-Response:**\n| λ | CAR Mean% | CAR SD | TSR Mean% | Seeds | Δ vs LoRA |\n|---|-----------|--------|-----------|-------|-----------|\n| 0 (LoRA) | 52.8 | 4.2 | 5.8 | 3 | ref |\n| 0.005 | 50.5 | 3.0 | 6.8 | 3 | −2.3 |\n| 0.01 | 52.7 | 0.3 | 7.0 | 3 | −0.1 |\n| 0.1 | 58.5 | 2.1 | 4.0 | 2 | +5.7 |\n\n**Phase 2 (10K SDF → 20K λ=0):** 2 seeds, mean CAR=59.5%, TSR=16.5%, Δ=+6.7pp vs LoRA, p=0.12\n**spatial_bowl:** SDF+LoRA CAR=35%, TSR=3%, but NO LoRA-only control (missing experiment)\n**dfCAR threshold:** Completely invariant across δ∈[2mm,100mm] due to 6-order-of-magnitude EE displacement gap\n\n## Experiment Design Reference (from review_context.yaml)\nThe full experiment plan included these experiments:\n- LoRA baseline eval (2 seeds) → completed\n- Phase 2 λ=0 training/eval (seed2) → completed  \n- spatial_bowl SDF training/eval → completed\n- Lambda=0.1 bracket (2 seeds) → completed\n- Phase 2 additional seed (seed0) → completed\n- LoRA seed2 → completed (CAR=48%, pulled 3-seed mean to 52.8%)\n- dfCAR threshold sensitivity → completed\n- **spatial_bowl LoRA-only control → NOT COMPLETED** (GPU resources exhausted)\n\nKey context: LoRA seed2 had CAR=48% (lower than s0=54.5, s1=56), increasing variance. The 3v3 comparison gives p=0.24 (one-sided) for LoRA vs SDF λ=0.005 — \"not statistically distinguishable but with suggestive trend.\"\n\n## Instructions\nWrite a detailed review covering:\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Strengths** (bulleted, focus on methods/experiments)\n3. **Weaknesses** (bulleted, focus on methods/experiments) \n4. **Questions for Authors** (specific, actionable)\n5. **Minor Issues**\n6. **Scores** (1-4 scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Accept, 4=Strong Accept) for: Overall, Soundness, Significance, Clarity, Confidence (1-4: 1=low, 4=expert)\n\nBe rigorous but fair. This is a primarily negative-result paper. Evaluate whether the evidence supports the claims."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":708,"cache_read_input_tokens":71342,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":708},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e6dd661-5539-4780-b46e-9be6f0e5cc6e","uuid":"b614b59b-a64d-4e52-bf1f-50714dd98e73"}
