oRA-only (p=0.24/0.48)\n- SDF λ=0.1: marginal +5.7pp (p=0.15), not significant\n- Phase 2 (SDF 10K→λ=0 20K): weak persistence +6.7pp (p=0.12), TSR=16.5%\n- ALL conditions: catastrophic TSR collapse 73%→4-7%\n\n**Related Work section (Section 2) covers:**\n- VLA models (Pi0, Pi0.5, OpenVLA) — brief\n- Collision avoidance in robotics (classical SDF, integration into learned policies) — brief\n- Safety evaluation metrics (CAR, SafeLIBERO) — brief\n\nThe paper has only 5 references total: Pi0, OpenVLA, SafeLIBERO, LoRA, CHOMP.\n\n**Section structure:**\n1. Introduction (1.5 pages)\n2. Related Work (0.5 page)\n3. Method (1 page): Problem setting, dfCAR definition, SDF auxiliary loss, LoRA fine-tuning\n4. Experiments (3 pages): Fake safety, dfCAR threshold, capability-safety anti-correlation, SDF structural limitation, fine-tuning attribution, lambda dose-response, Phase 2 persistence\n5. Discussion (1.5 pages)\n6. Conclusion (0.5 page)\n\n**Limitations acknowledged by authors:**\n(i) Only SafeLIBERO with Pi0/Pi0.5 — generalizability unknown\n(ii) n=3 seeds, limited statistical power\n(iii) spatial_bowl missing LoRA-only control\n(iv) Only EE-only SDF evaluated, not full-body SDF\n(v) Phase 2 based on 2 seeds — preliminary\n\n## Experiment Coverage Assessment\nFrom the experiment design (review_context.yaml), the paper covers most planned experiments EXCEPT:\n- spatial_bowl LoRA-only control (NOT COMPLETED — GPU resources exhausted) → cannot do cross-scene SDF attribution\n\nThe paper's narrative was adjusted from \"clean negative\" to \"predominantly negative with boundary conditions\" due to: LoRA seed2 pulling down the 3-seed mean, making the \"SDF = LoRA\" claim weaker (p=0.24 instead of clearly indistinguishable).\n\n## Instructions\nWrite a detailed review covering:\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Strengths** (bulleted, focus on novelty/positioning/writing/impact)\n3. **Weaknesses** (bulleted, focus on novelty/related work/positioning/missing comparisons)\n4. **Questions for Authors** (specific, actionable)\n5. **Minor Issues**\n6. **Scores** (1-4 scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Accept, 4=Strong Accept) for: Overall, Novelty, Significance, Clarity, Confidence (1-4: 1=low, 4=expert)\n\nBe rigorous but fair. Consider: Is this paper a meaningful contribution to the robot learning community? Is the \"fake safety\" finding genuinely novel or widely known? Is dfCAR a real contribution or trivially obvious? Are the SDF redundancy claims sufficiently supported? Is the related work adequate?","uuid":"82759208-351e-4f87-aa6a-340fa7079ba3","session_id":"2e6dd661-5539-4780-b46e-9be6f0e5cc6e"}
