{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AyxrHBfbtGx6465mofh2Bk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tmeta:\n2\t  venue: \"CoRL 2026 / ICRA 2027\"\n3\t  track: main\n4\t  template: templates/latex/corl2026/\n5\t  template_note: \"需确认 CoRL 2026 官方模板; fallback CoRL 2025\"\n6\t  page_limit: 8\n7\t  deadline: 2026-06-13\n8\t  working_title: \"The Safety Illusion: How Action Collapse Contaminates Collision Avoidance Metrics in Vision-Language-Action Models\"\n9\t  core_claim: >\n10\t    VLA safety 评估存在系统性缺陷：collision avoidance rate (CAR) 被 action collapse 严重污染。\n11\t    我们通过大规模实证分析（39 experiments, 5000+ episodes）揭示 fake safety 现象，\n12\t    提出 displacement-filtered CAR 作为修正指标，并展示 training-time SDF auxiliary supervision\n13\t    在能力充分的 VLA 上产生真实碰撞避免行为（pending Claim 4）。\n14\t  paper_type: analysis  # analysis paper with (pending) positive method contribution\n15\t  created_at: 2026-05-24T14:00:00Z\n16\t  supersedes: \"ColliForce-VLA method paper (writing_plan v1, 2026-05-20)\"\n17\t\n18\tpaper_outline:\n19\t  - section: abstract\n20\t    word_budget: 200\n21\t    core_bullets:\n22\t      - \"问题：VLA collision avoidance 中 CAR 被 action collapse 污染——高 CAR ≠ 真正碰撞避免\"\n23\t      - \"发现 1：91.5% CAR 中 99.6% 是 fake safe (robot displacement < 0.1mm)\"\n24\t      - \"发现 2：TSR-CAR 反相关——能力越强的 VLA 碰撞越多 (Pi0.5 TSR=74.7% CAR=26.8%)\"\n25\t      - \"发现 3：EE-only SDF 存在结构性缺陷——GT oracle 均劣于 baseline\"\n26\t      - \"贡献：displacement-filtered CAR 指标 + [Claim 4 placeholder: SDF aux on Pi0.5]\"\n27\t    dependencies: [analysis_claim1, analysis_claim2, analysis_claim3, experimental_framework]\n28\t\n29\t  - section: introduction\n30\t    word_budget: 1200\n31\t    core_bullets:\n32\t      - \"Hook: VLA safety 是部署核心障碍; SafeLIBERO 系统量化碰撞问题; 多个方法报告高 CAR\"\n33\t      - \"Problem: 高 CAR 可能是 'safety illusion'——action collapse 让 robot 停止运动而非绕开障碍物\"\n34\t      - \"Finding 1: A1 SDF aux loss 报告 91.5% CAR, 但 99.6% 来自 displacement < 0.1mm 的 frozen episodes\"\n35\t      - \"Finding 2: Pi0.5 (TSR=74.7%) vs Pi0 (TSR≈0%): 能力越强→运动越多→碰撞越多. 'High CAR' on Pi0 = inability to move\"\n36\t      - \"Finding 3: 3 组 GT SDF oracle refinement 均劣于 baseline, fake_safe 仍 96-98%——EE-only SDF 结构性不足\"\n37\t      - \"Solution: displacement-filtered CAR (CAR_f) 指标——仅计算 displacement > threshold 的 episode\"\n38\t      - \"Contributions: [C1] fake safety phenomenon + CAR_f metric; [C2] capability-safety anti-correlation; [C3] EE-only structural limitation + oracle evidence; [C4 placeholder] SDF aux on capable VLA\"\n39\t    dependencies: [analysis_claim1]\n40\t    citation_hints:\n41\t      - \"SafeLIBERO/AEGIS (Hu et al. 2025) — benchmark + existing safety method\"\n42\t      - \"SafeVLA (Zhang et al. 2025) — RL-based safety\"\n43\t      - \"π0 (Black et al. 2024) — base architecture\"\n44\t      - \"CoFreeVLA (2026) — dual-arm safety\"\n45\t\n46\t  - section: related_work\n47\t    word_budget: 700\n48\t    core_bullets:\n49\t      - \"§2.1 Collision-Safe VLA: AEGIS CBF post-hoc, SafeVLA CMDP, CoFreeVLA risk estimator, CAPE inference-time, iKinQP-RL QP correction, Li et al. cost-guided denoising → 共同点: 报告 CAR 但未检验 metric validity\"\n50\t      - \"§2.2 SDF in Robotics: DeepSDF, iSDF, DiffCo, VoxPoser, SAMP → SDF 用于碰撞检测/规划, 我们揭示 EE-only SDF 在 VLA 中的结构性限制\"\n51\t      - \"§2.3 Evaluation Reliability in Robot Learning: metric gaming / benchmark saturation 文献 → 我们将 metric contamination 问题带入 VLA safety 评估领域\"\n52\t    dependencies: [introduction]\n53\t\n54\t  - section: experimental_framework\n55\t    label: \"Experimental Framework\"\n56\t    word_budget: 900\n57\t    core_bullets:\n58\t      - \"§3.1 Benchmark & Models: SafeLIBERO object_pudding (4 tasks, Level I); Pi0 (openpi) + Pi0.5 基座; Full-FT / LoRA / A1-SDF 训练方案; evaluation protocol (50 ep/task)\"\n59\t      - \"§3.2 Standard Metrics: CAR (collision avoidance rate), TSR (task success rate) — 定义 + SafeLIBERO 原始公式\"\n60\t      - \"§3.3 Displacement-Filtered CAR (CAR_f): 核心方法论贡献. 定义 action collapse (max displacement < τ_d=0.1mm). CAR_f = safe episodes with displacement ≥ τ_d / total non-collapsed episodes. Motivation: CAR 不区分 'safe because avoided' vs 'safe because frozen'\"\n61\t      - \"§3.4 SDF Auxiliary Training (A1): SDF Decoder (4-layer MLP, ~395K params) + EE Extractor (2-layer MLP, ~263K params); SDF loss + EE loss as auxiliary objectives; LoRA fine-tuning on π0/π0.5. 为 Claims 1,3,4 提供实验方法\"\n62\t      - \"§3.5 Oracle SDF Refinement: GT SDF gradient-based action refinement at inference (3 variants: adaptive α, fixed α, feature-space). 为 Claim 3 提供 upper bound 实验设计\"\n63\t    dependencies: []\n64\t    notation_table:\n65\t      \"CAR\": \"Collision Avoidance Rate — fraction of episodes without collision\"\n66\t      \"CAR_f\": \"Displacement-Filtered CAR — excludes action-collapsed episodes\"\n67\t      \"TSR\": \"Task Success Rate\"\n68\t      \"SSR\": \"Simultaneous Success Rate (TSR ∩ CAR)\"\n69\t      \"d_max(τ)\": \"Maximum EE displacement in episode τ\"\n70\t      \"τ_d\": \"Displacement threshold = 0.1mm\"\n71\t      \"Φ(x)\": \"Signed distance at point x (>0 free, =0 surface, <0 penetration)\"\n72\t      \"f_SDF\": \"SDF Decoder — 4-layer MLP predicting workspace SDF from VLA features\"\n73\t      \"f_EE\": \"EE Extractor — 2-layer MLP predicting end-effector position\"\n74\t      \"λ_SDF\": \"SDF auxiliary loss weight\"\n75\t\n76\t  - section: analysis_claim1\n77\t    label: \"The Fake Safety Problem\"\n78\t    word_budget: 650\n79\t    core_bullets:\n80\t      - \"§4.1 (or §5.1): Fake Safety is Pervasive\"\n81\t      - \"A1-LoRA (Pi0) 800ep: CAR=91.5%, 但 732 safe episodes 中 729 (99.6%) displacement < 0.1mm\"\n82\t      - \"Displacement histogram: 73.9% < 1µm, 25.7% 1µm-0.1mm, 0.4% 0.1mm-1mm, 0% > 1mm\"\n83\t      - \"LoRA baseline 200ep: CAR=82%, fake_safe=99.4% — fake safety 不是 A1 特有, 是 action collapse 通病\"\n84\t      - \"Pi0.5 baseline: safe episodes 中 98.2% 也是 fake (仅 s0 数据)\"\n85\t      - \"displacement-filtered CAR: 所有 Pi0 方法 → CAR_f ≈ 0%; Pi0.5 baseline → CAR_f ≈ 0.5%\"\n86\t      - \"Table 1 (tab1_fake_safety): 跨方法 fake safety 统计全景\"\n87\t      - \"Fig 2 (fig2_displacement): displacement 分布直方图, 0.1mm 阈值标注\"\n88\t    dependencies: [experimental_framework]\n89\t    data_source: \"paper_data_summary Table 2 + A1 displacement distribution\"\n90\t\n91\t  - section: analysis_claim2\n92\t    label: \"Capability-Safety Anti-correlation\"\n93\t    word_budget: 400\n94\t    core_bullets:\n95\t      - \"§4.2 (or §5.2): More Capable Models Collide More\"\n96\t      - \"Pi0.5 3-seed: TSR=74.7±1.5%, CAR=26.8±1.6% (n=600)\"\n97\t      - \"Pi0 baselines: TSR≈0%, CAR=82-83% — high CAR 来自 inability to move\"\n98\t      - \"TSR-CAR scatter plot (Fig 3): Pi0 系聚集左上角 (fake safety zone), Pi0.5 baseline 右下\"\n99\t      - \"Framing: observation, not causal claim. 机制: 能力→运动→接近障碍物→碰撞\"\n100\t      - \"Implication: CAR 单独不足以评估 safety, 必须与 TSR 联合解读\"\n101\t    dependencies: [analysis_claim1]\n102\t    data_source: \"paper_data_summary Table 4 scatter data\"\n103\t\n104\t  - section: analysis_claim3\n105\t    label: \"EE-Only SDF Structural Limitation\"\n106\t    word_budget: 600\n107\t    core_bullets:\n108\t      - \"§4.3 (or §5.3): End-Effector-Only SDF Cannot Ensure Full-Body Safety\"\n109\t      - \"3 oracle variants (all use GT SDF): adaptive CAR=75%, fixed CAR=73.1%, feature CAR=76.9%\"\n110\t      - \"所有 oracle 均 < baseline CAR=82%; fake_safe_rate 仍 96-98%\"\n111\t      - \"根因: SDF gradient 推 EE 远离障碍物, 但 arm body 可能被推向障碍物\"\n112\t      - \"Feature-space oracle: 每步 241.7 refinements (vs action-space 14.2), gradient 幅度极小 (0.004-0.006), 效果无显著差异\"\n113\t      - \"Per-task CAR 分解: task1 (chocolate_pudding) 是所有方法难点\"\n114\t      - \"Oracle bar chart (Fig 4): 3 variants + baselines, overlay fake_safe_rate\"\n115\t      - \"Table 3 (tab3_oracle): 完整数据\"\n116\t    dependencies: [analysis_claim1]\n117\t    data_source: \"paper_data_summary Table 3 + per-task data\"\n118\t\n119\t  - section: analysis_claim4_placeholder\n120\t    label: \"[PLACEHOLDER] SDF Auxiliary Loss on Capable VLA\"\n121\t    word_budget: 250\n122\t    core_bullets:\n123\t      - \"§4.4 (or §5.4): 10K Preview — First Evidence of Real Collision Avoidance\"\n124\t      - \"Pi0.5+A1 s0: λ=0.005 CAR=58%, λ=0.01 CAR=56.5%; TSR=47-49%; frozen_rate=0%\"\n125\t      - \"与 baseline 对比: CAR +30pp, TSR -26pp, 0% frozen → first method with non-fake safety\"\n126\t      - \"[TODO: 30K 3-seed × 2-lambda 完整结果]\"\n127\t      - \"[TODO: LoRA baseline 对比 — 归因 SDF vs LoRA capacity]\"\n128\t      - \"[TODO: Task-dependent tradeoff 分析 (Task 0-2 up, Task 3 down)]\"\n129\t    dependencies: [analysis_claim1, analysis_claim2, analysis_claim3]\n130\t    data_source: \"ROADMAP D016 + pending 30K eval\"\n131\t\n132\t  - section: conclusion_placeholder\n133\t    label: \"[PLACEHOLDER] Discussion & Conclusion\"\n134\t    word_budget: 300\n135\t    core_bullets:\n136\t      - \"[PLACEHOLDER] 等 Claim 4 完整数据\"\n137\t      - \"Summary: fake safety pervasive → CAR_f metric → EE-only limitation → [Claim 4]\"\n138\t      - \"Implications for VLA safety evaluation community\"\n139\t      - \"Limitations: SafeLIBERO only, 2 model families (Pi0/Pi0.5), single task suite (object_pudding)\"\n140\t      - \"Future: full-body SDF, additional VLA architectures, real-robot validation, standardized safety benchmarks\"\n141\t    dependencies: [analysis_claim4_placeholder]\n142\t\n143\tvisualization_plan:\n144\t  - fig_id: fig1_concept\n145\t    type: conceptual\n146\t    tool: paperbanana\n147\t    description: \"Fake vs real safety 概念图 — 左: fake safe (frozen robot, misleading ✓), 右: real safe (robot navigating around obstacle, genuine ✓)\"\n148\t    narrative_intent: \"一图说明核心概念: 高 CAR 不等于碰撞避免, displacement 才是区分 fake/real safety 的关键\"\n149\t    design_notes:\n150\t      - \"两面板对比: 左=frozen robot + 'Safe ✓' label + 'displacement ≈ 0', 右=robot avoiding + 'Safe ✓' + 'displacement > τ'\"\n151\t      - \"左面板加红色警告: 'Action Collapse'\"\n152\t      - \"底部示意: standard CAR counts both → CAR_f filters left panel\"\n153\t      - \"简洁, 顶会品质, 不是 tutorial diagram\"\n154\t    placement: introduction\n155\t    aspect_ratio: \"16:9\"\n156\t    priority: important\n157\t\n158\t  - fig_id: fig2_displacement\n159\t    type: statistical\n160\t    tool: matplotlib\n161\t    description: \"Displacement 分布直方图 — A1-LoRA (800ep) + LoRA baseline (200ep), log-scale, 0.1mm threshold\"\n162\t    narrative_intent: \"99.6% safe episodes 的 displacement < 0.1mm → CAR 被 action collapse 严重污染\"\n163\t    design_notes:\n164\t      - \"Log-scale x-axis (displacement), count on y-axis\"\n165\t      - \"Vertical dashed line at τ_d = 0.1mm with annotation\"\n166\t      - \"Left of threshold: red/pink fill (fake safe zone)\"\n167\t      - \"Right of threshold: green fill (real safe zone)\"\n168\t      - \"A1 800ep 数据: <1µm: 541, 1µm-0.1mm: 188, 0.1mm-1mm: 3, >1mm: 0\"\n169\t      - \"可选: 叠加 Pi0.5 baseline 的 displacement 分布做对比\"\n170\t      - \"NO matplotlib defaults. 白背景, 精细字号, 专业配色\"\n171\t    data_source: \"paper_data_summary: A1-LoRA displacement bins\"\n172\t    placement: analysis_claim1\n173\t    aspect_ratio: \"4:3\"\n174\t    priority: must\n175\t\n176\t  - fig_id: fig3_tsr_car_scatter\n177\t    type: statistical\n178\t    tool: matplotlib\n179\t    description: \"TSR vs CAR scatter — 全方法对比, 区分 fake/real safe\"\n180\t    narrative_intent: \"Pi0 系方法聚集左上角 (fake safety zone); Pi0.5+A1 唯一向右上移动且 0% frozen\"\n181\t    design_notes:\n182\t      - \"X=TSR [0,1], Y=CAR [0,1]\"\n183\t      - \"Shaded region upper-left: 'Fake Safety Zone' (high CAR, low TSR)\"\n184\t      - \"Hollow markers: fake-safe-dominated methods (Pi0 系)\"\n185\t      - \"Filled markers: real-safe methods (Pi0.5+A1)\"\n186\t      - \"Pi0.5 baseline: filled blue circles\"\n187\t      - \"Annotate key clusters with method family names\"\n188\t      - \"Star marker for Pi0.5+A1 (the promising direction)\"\n189\t      - \"Data from paper_data_summary Table 4\"\n190\t    data_source: \"paper_data_summary: Table 4 scatter data points\"\n191\t    placement: analysis_claim2\n192\t    aspect_ratio: \"1:1\"\n193\t    priority: important\n194\t\n195\t  - fig_id: fig4_oracle_bar\n196\t    type: statistical\n197\t    tool: matplotlib\n198\t    description: \"Oracle refinement CAR comparison — 3 GT SDF oracle variants + baselines\"\n199\t    narrative_intent: \"即使 GT SDF + oracle refinement 也无法提升 CAR 超过 baseline → EE-only 结构性缺陷\"\n200\t    design_notes:\n201\t      - \"Grouped bars: x=methods, y=CAR\"\n202\t      - \"Baseline (gray): LoRA 82%, Full-FT 83%\"\n203\t      - \"Oracle (green shades): adaptive 75%, fixed 73.1%, feature 76.9%\"\n204\t      - \"A1 (orange): 91.5% (但标注 '99.6% fake')\"\n205\t      - \"Horizontal dashed line at baseline CAR\"\n206\t      - \"Secondary info: fake_safe_rate annotation above each bar\"\n207\t      - \"Message: oracle CAR < baseline CAR, and all nearly 100% fake\"\n208\t    data_source: \"paper_data_summary: Table 3\"\n209\t    placement: analysis_claim3\n210\t    aspect_ratio: \"4:3\"\n211\t    priority: must\n212\t\n213\ttable_plan:\n214\t  - table_id: tab1_fake_safety\n215\t    caption: \"Fake safety analysis. Standard CAR appears high, but displacement-filtered CAR reveals that 96-99.6\\\\% of 'safe' episodes involve action collapse (displacement < 0.1mm).\"\n216\t    placement: analysis_claim1\n217\t    type: analysis\n218\t    columns: [Method, Episodes, TSR, CAR, \"Fake Rate\", \"CAR_f\"]\n219\t    data_source: \"paper_data_summary Table 2\"\n220\t    notes: \"CAR_f = displacement-filtered CAR (proposed metric). Fake Rate = fraction of safe episodes with displacement < τ_d.\"\n221\t\n222\t  - table_id: tab2_pi05_a1_placeholder\n223\t    caption: \"[PLACEHOLDER] Pi0.5 + SDF auxiliary loss (3-seed × 2-lambda). Pending 30K evaluation.\"\n224\t    placement: analysis_claim4_placeholder\n225\t    type: comparison\n226\t    columns: [Config, TSR, CAR, \"Frozen Rate\", \"CAR_f\"]\n227\t    data_source: \"ROADMAP D016 (10K preview) + pending 30K eval\"\n228\t\n229\t  - table_id: tab3_oracle\n230\t    caption: \"Oracle SDF refinement with ground-truth distance fields. All three variants achieve lower CAR than unrefined baselines, and fake safe rates remain above 96\\\\%.\"\n231\t    placement: analysis_claim3\n232\t    type: comparison\n233\t    columns: [Method, TSR, CAR, \"Fake Rate\", \"Refines/ep\"]\n234\t    data_source: \"paper_data_summary Table 3\"\n235\t\n236\tliterature_strategy:\n237\t  citation_budget: 30\n238\t  macro_context:\n239\t    - \"VLA safety and collision avoidance\"\n240\t    - \"signed distance fields in robot manipulation\"\n241\t    - \"evaluation metric reliability in robot learning / ML\"\n242\t    - \"action collapse and mode collapse in generative policies\"\n243\t  micro_clusters:\n244\t    - cluster_name: \"collision-aware-vla\"\n245\t      search_queries:\n246\t        - \"collision avoidance vision language action model 2024 2025 2026\"\n247\t        - \"safe VLA manipulation policy constraint\"\n248\t      must_cite:\n249\t        - \"AEGIS/VLSA (Hu et al. 2025)\"\n250\t        - \"SafeVLA (Zhang et al. 2025)\"\n251\t        - \"CoFreeVLA (2026)\"\n252\t      target_count: 6\n253\t\n254\t    - cluster_name: \"sdf-robotics\"\n255\t      search_queries:\n256\t        - \"signed distance field robot collision differentiable 2021 2022 2023 2024\"\n257\t      must_cite:\n258\t        - \"DeepSDF (Park et al. 2019)\"\n259\t        - \"DiffCo (Zhi et al. 2021)\"\n260\t      target_count: 4\n261\t\n262\t    - cluster_name: \"vla-foundation\"\n263\t      must_cite:\n264\t        - \"π0 (Black et al. 2024)\"\n265\t        - \"OpenVLA (Kim et al. 2024)\"\n266\t        - \"LIBERO (Liu et al. 2023)\"\n267\t      target_count: 4\n268\t\n269\t    - cluster_name: \"metric-reliability\"\n270\t      search_queries:\n271\t        - \"evaluation metric reliability robot learning benchmark 2023 2024 2025\"\n272\t        - \"benchmark saturation gaming machine learning evaluation\"\n273\t        - \"safety metric validity robotics\"\n274\t      must_cite: []\n275\t      target_count: 4\n276\t\n277\t    - cluster_name: \"action-collapse\"\n278\t      search_queries:\n279\t        - \"action collapse VLA policy mode collapse frozen 2024 2025\"\n280\t        - \"mode collapse diffusion policy degenerate behavior\"\n281\t        - \"action repetition failure mode learned policy\"\n282\t      must_cite: []\n283\t      target_count: 3\n284\t\n285\twriting_order:\n286\t  - analysis_claim1      # Fake Safety — core finding, sets up everything\n287\t  - analysis_claim2      # TSR-CAR anti-correlation\n288\t  - analysis_claim3      # EE-only limitation\n289\t  - experimental_framework  # Method/setup — informed by what results need\n290\t  - introduction          # Narrative wrapper\n291\t  - related_work          # Positioning\n292\t  - abstract              # Distillation\n293\t  - analysis_claim4_placeholder  # Brief placeholder\n294\t  - conclusion_placeholder       # Brief placeholder\n295\t\n296\tcolor_palette:\n297\t  baseline_pi0: \"#808080\"       # gray — Pi0 baselines (action collapsed)\n298\t  baseline_pi05: \"#0072B2\"      # blue — Pi0.5 baselines (capable but unsafe)\n299\t  a1_sdf: \"#E69F00\"             # orange — A1 SDF methods\n300\t  oracle: \"#009E73\"             # green — Oracle variants\n301\t  pi05_a1: \"#D55E00\"            # vermillion — Pi0.5+A1 (promising)\n302\t  fake_zone: \"#FFCCCC\"          # light red — fake safety zone\n303\t  real_zone: \"#CCFFCC\"          # light green — real safety zone\n304\t  threshold_line: \"#CC0000\"     # dark red — displacement threshold\n305\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013nCxBRTTrC7C4kDzoJmBr2","session_id":"2e6dd661-5539-4780-b46e-9be6f0e5cc6e","uuid":"d315e84f-8ba9-46a1-ba43-3a67772b4a12","timestamp":"2026-05-26T03:28:54.231Z"}
